    {
      "label": "Recommendations for the Grouping of Wards into District Electoral Areas for the purpose of Local Government Elections in Northern Ireland: Report by the District Electoral Areas Commissioner, Dr Maurice Hayes (Belfast: HMSO, December 1992)",
      "note": "Final recommendations. Appendix I lists each district electoral area with its wards and its electorate on the 1991 register; OSNI printed the same figures as \"Area Electorate\" on the four final-recommendation maps (Local Government District Electoral Areas: 1992, Maps 1-4, Final Recommendations). Each area on this map carries its figure (dea1992_electorate); the 101 sum to 1,132,617 and every district agrees with the printed district electorate. 90 areas are unchanged from the provisional recommendations of 20 August 1992; in Ballymena (Ballymena North 12,004; Ballymena South 12,151; Bannside 8,964; Braid 8,722), Carrickfergus (Knockagh Monument 8,426; Kilroot 8,696; Carrick Castle 6,847), Magherafelt (Magherafelt Town 9,303; Moyola 7,930) and Strabane (Mourne 9,619; Derg 8,055) the final groupings and figures differ, and Coleraine West was renamed Coleraine Central (10,194). Printed report; no online copy found."
    },
    {
      "label": "District Electoral Areas (Northern Ireland) Order 1993 (S.I. 1993 No. 226)",
